{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "ASV1901",
  "book_code": "JOB",
  "chapter": 11,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JOB.11.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.11.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then answered Zophar the Naamathite, and said,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.11.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.11.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Should not the multitude of words be answered?\nAnd should a man full of talk be justified?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.11.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.11.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Should thy boastings make men hold their peace?\nAnd when thou mockest, shall no man make thee ashamed?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.11.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.11.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For thou sayest, My doctrine is pure,\nAnd I am clean in thine eyes.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.11.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.11.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But oh that God would speak,\nAnd open his lips against thee,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.11.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.11.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And that he would show thee the secrets of wisdom!\nFor he is manifold in understanding.\nKnow therefore that God exacteth of thee less than thine iniquity deserveth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.11.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.11.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Canst thou by searching find out God?\nCanst thou find out the Almighty unto perfection?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.11.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.11.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "It is high as heaven; what canst thou do?\nDeeper than Sheol; what canst thou know?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.11.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.11.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The measure thereof is longer than the earth,\nAnd broader than the sea.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.11.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.11.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If he pass through, and shut up,\nAnd call unto judgment, then who can hinder him?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.11.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.11.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For he knoweth false men:\nHe seeth iniquity also, even though he consider it not.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.11.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.11.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But vain man is void of understanding,\nYea, man is born ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a wild ass’s colt.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.11.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.11.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If thou set thy heart aright,\nAnd stretch out thy hands toward him;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.11.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.11.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If iniquity be in thy hand, put it far away,\nAnd let not unrighteousness dwell in thy tents.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.11.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.11.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Surely then shalt thou lift up thy face without spot;\nYea, thou shalt be stedfast, and shalt not fear:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.11.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.11.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For thou shalt forget thy misery;\nThou shalt remember it as waters that are passed away,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.11.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.11.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thy",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " life shall be clearer than the noonday;\nThough there be darkness, it shall be as the morning.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.11.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.11.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And thou shalt be secure, because there is hope;\nYea, thou shalt search ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "about thee",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and shalt take thy rest in safety.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.11.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.11.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Also thou shalt lie down, and none shall make thee afraid;\nYea, many shall make suit unto thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.11.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.11.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But the eyes of the wicked shall fail,\nAnd they shall have no way to flee;\nAnd their hope shall be the giving up of the ghost.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    }
  ]
}
